                <pb facs="0855" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg749"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Earl of Elgin to
                        Governor Sir W. MacGregor.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegraphic]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Downing Street</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-10-06"><hi rendition="#italic">October 6,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 43.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Referring to your telegram of the 5th instant, His Majesty’s ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Brilliant</hi> has been ordered to remain in
                    Newfoundland waters until end of season.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
